1.what is modelling.why we use it.why it is important?
  Modelling means the process of creating relationships between tables,so that powerbi can analyse data correctly,it helps to create accurate reports

2.what is relationships
  Relationship is a connection between two tables using a common column
  we have 4 types of relationships
  1.one-one
  2.one-many
  3.many-many
  4.many-one

3.what is cardinality
  cardinality means relation between two tables
  It defines the type of relationship
  we have 4 types of relationships
  1.one-one  
  2.one-many
  3.many-many
  4.many-one

4.what is starschema 
  starschema means one fact table connected to multiple dimension table
  fact table is at center connected to surrounding multiple dimension tables

5.what is fact and dimension tables.Explain its difference
  Fact tables contains numeric values,that can be change 
  fact table is at center connected to dimension tables
  ex: sales amount,quantity,profit,cost
  Dimension table contains descriptive information and it is static,that cann't be changed
  we have multiple dimension tables connected to one fact table
  ex: customer name,product name,location,date
        Fact table                            Dimension table
   stores transcations                     stores descriptions
   contain numeric values                  contain text/details
    ex: salesamount                           ex:customername
